Package: rnaparallel
Type: Package
Title: Exact Parallel Companions for 'sva' ComBat-Seq, 'edgeR' and 'limma'
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("GenomeRx", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "author of the parallel companions"),
    person("Nam", "Nguyen", email = "namnguyenhk@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Yuqing", "Zhang", role = "ctb",
           comment = "author of ComBat-seq, accelerated but not modified by this package"),
    person("Giovanni", "Parmigiani", role = "ctb", comment = "author of ComBat-seq"),
    person("W. Evan", "Johnson", role = "ctb", comment = "author of ComBat-seq"))
Description: Provides parallel companions to five RNA-seq steps that are slow
    at cohort scale and take no worker argument: ComBat_seq() from 'sva',
    normLibSizes() from 'edgeR', and lmFit(), duplicateCorrelation() and
    removeBatchEffect() from 'limma'. Each calls the original function
    unmodified, with its slow internal helpers rebound in a child of the
    original's environment, and splits work by gene, sample or batch only
    where each piece reads its own slice plus values computed once from the
    whole input. The result is identical() to the original's, so the next
    step reads it unchanged. Backends are mclapply(), 'future',
    'BiocParallel', 'foreach' and serial. A memory guard lowers the worker
    count when available memory is short.
